Tue Aug  4 10:02:49 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package (version 1.3.0)
- Model Context Protocol server for Slack, exposing conversations,
  channel and user directories, message history and search to MCP
  capable clients over the stdio and server-sent-events transports
- Authenticates with existing Slack session tokens or an OAuth user
  token, so no workspace app installation is required
- Do not pass upstream's "-s -w" link flags, which would strip the
  symbol table and leave the debuginfo subpackage empty
- Skip the TestIntegration cases in %%check: they drive a live Slack
  workspace and an OpenAI endpoint, and fail rather than skip when
  the credentials are absent
- Exclude the container, editor and npm redistribution plumbing from
  the source tarball, none of which is used to build or run the server

